<title>USA: Tele-Communications to buy DMX Inc.</title>
<headline>Tele-Communications to buy DMX Inc.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc said on Friday it agreed definitively to buy DMX Inc in a stock swap and will make it a unit of TCI Music Inc, a newly formed Tele-Communications subsidiary.</p>
<p>Each DMX share would be converted into a half-share of TCI Music. Former DMX shareholders would have the right to sell their new shares back to TCI for $4 per share under certain conditions.</p>
<p>Tele-Communications' acquisition of DMX must be approved by regulators and DMX shareholders.  </p>
<p>DMX stockholders would own 19.25 percent of TCI Music and TCI and its affiliates would hold the remaining 80.75 percent.</p>
</text>
